a - MA', 'Sampaio Corrêa - MA']\n  'santa cruz': ['Santa Cruz', 'Santa Cruz - PE', 'Santa Cruz - RN', 'Santa Cruz - RS', 'Santa Cruz RN', 'Santa Cruz RS', 'Santa Cruz-PE']\n  'santa rita': ['Santa Rita', 'Santa Rita - AL']\n  'santo andre': ['Santo Andre', 'Santo Andre SP', 'Santo André', 'Santo André - SP']\n  'santos': ['Santos', 'Santos - AP', 'Santos - SP', 'Santos AP', 'Santos-SP']\n  'sao bento': ['Sao Bento', 'São Bento - SP']\n  'sao bernardo': ['Sao Bernardo', 'Sao Bernardo - SP']\n  'sao caetano': ['Sao Caetano', 'São Caetano', 'São Caetano - SP']\n  'sao francisco': ['Sao Francisco AC', 'Sao Francisco PA']\n  'sao jose': ['Sao Jose PA', 'Sao Jose RS', 'São José - RS']\n  'sao luiz': ['Sao Luiz', 'Sao Luiz - RS', 'São Luiz - RS']\n  'sao paulo': ['Sao Paulo', 'Sao Paulo-SP', 'São Paulo', 'São Paulo - SP']\n  'sao raimundo': ['Sao Raimundo AM', 'Sao Raimundo PA', 'Sao Raimundo RR', 'São Raimundo - PA', 'São Raimundo - RR']\n  'sergipe': ['Sergipe', 'Sergipe - SE']\n  'sobradinho': ['Sobradinho', 'Sobradinho - DF']\n  'sport': ['Sport', 'Sport - PE', 'Sport-PE']\n  'tocantinopolis': ['Tocantinopolis', 'Tocantinópolis - TO']\n  'tombense': ['Tombense', 'Tombense - MG', 'Tombense MG']\n  'trem': ['Trem - AP', 'Trem AP']\n  'treze': ['Treze', 'Treze - PB']\n  'tubarao': ['Tubarao', 'Tubarão - SC']\n  'tupi': ['Tupi', 'Tupi - MG', 'Tupi MG']\n  'uberlandia': ['Uberlandia', 'Uberlândia - MG']\n  'uniclinic': ['Uniclinic - CE', 'Uniclinic CE']\n  'urt': ['URT', 'URT MG', 'Urt - MG']\n  'vasco da gama': ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Vasco da Gama - RJ', 'Vasco da Gama-RJ']\n  'vila nova': ['Vila Nova', 'Vila Nova - GO']\n  'vilhena': ['Vilhena - RO', 'Vilhena RO']\n  'villa nova': ['Villa Nova', 'Villa Nova - MG']\n  'vitoria': ['Vitoria', 'Vitoria ES', 'Vitoria-BA', 'Vitória', 'Vitória - BA']\n  'vitoria da conquista': ['Vitoria da Conquista', 'Vitória da Conquista - BA']\n  'volta redonda': ['Volta Redonda', 'Volta Redonda - RJ']\n  'ypiranga': ['Ypiranga', 'Ypiranga - AP', 'Ypiranga - RS', 'Ypiranga AP', 'Ypiranga RS']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-809922ee1cb6 && venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', t).encode('ascii','ignore').decode()\n    t = re.sub(r'\\(.*?\\)', ' ', t)\n    t = re.sub(r'\\bantigo\\b', ' ', t)\n    t = t.replace('-', ' ')\n    t = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', t).strip().lower()\n    return t\n\nUFS = {'sp','rj','mg','rs','pr','sc','ba','pe','ce','go','mt','ms','df','pa','am','rn','pb','se','al','ma','pi','to','ro','rr','ap','es','ac'}\n\nnames = Counter()\nfiles = {\n 'brasileirao': ('home_team','away_team'),\n 'copa': ('home_team','away_team'),\n 'lib': ('home_team','away_team'),\n 'brfootball': ('home','away'),\n 'novo': ('Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante'),\n}\nfnames = {'brasileirao':'Brasileirao_Matches.csv','copa':'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','lib':'Libertadores_Matches.csv','brfootball':'BR-Football-Dataset.csv','novo':'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv'}\nper_file = {}\nfor key,(hc,ac) in files.items():\n    c = Counter()\n    with open('data/kaggle/'+fnames[key], encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            c[row[hc]] += 1; c[row[ac]] += 1\n    per_file[key] = set(c)\n    names.update(c)\n\n# Show names that after UF-stripping collide\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nstripped = defaultdict(set)\nfor raw in names:\n    n = norm(raw)\n    toks = n.split()\n    if len(toks) > 1 and toks[-1] in UFS:\n        base = ' '.join(toks[:-1])\n    else:\n        base = n\n    stripped[base].add(raw)\ncollisions = {b:v for b,v in stripped.items() if len(v)>1}\nprint('COLLIDING BASES (UF-stripped):', len(collisions))\nfor b, v in sorted(collisions.items()):\n    print(f'  {b!r}: {sorted(v)}')\n\"","time":{"start":1788282284422,"end":1788282284425}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There's a problem: \"atletico\" is ambiguous — in 2019, both Atlético-MG and Athletico-PR play in Série A, but my normalization collapses \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Athletico-PR\" both to... wait no. \"Atlético-MG\" → strip accents → \"Atletico-MG\" → strip UF \"mg\" → \"atletico\". \"Athletico-PR\" → \"athletico pr\" → wait accents: Athletico has no accent. Hmm \"Athletico-PR\" → \"athletico\" too? No — \"athletico-pr\" → strip \"pr\" → \"athletico\". That's different from \"atletico\".\n\nBut the results show \"atletico\" with 112 pts in 2019 — that's wrong. Flamengo won 2019 with 90. The issue: \"Atlético-GO\" also normalizes to \"atletico\" (stripping -GO)! And in 2018 \"Atlético-MG\" (champion, 80 pts) + \"Atlético-GO\" (also in Série A 2018?) both → \"atletico\" → merged 116.\n\nSo stripping UF suffixes is WRONG for teams whose name is just \"Atlético-XX\" — the state IS the disambiguator. Atlético-MG, Atlético-GO, Athletico-PR, Atlético-PR are different clubs.\n\nBetter strategy: only strip a UF suffix when the remaining name is a \"known multi-word team\" or when the suffix follows a name that doesn't already end in something ambiguous... Actually the cleanest: maintain a curated canonical team registry. There are a manageable number of relevant teams (Série A/B clubs + Libertadores participants). Let me think.\n\nApproach: normalization pipeline produces a key; but for UF-suffixed names, keep the UF as part of the key UNLESS the base name is unique enough to identify... Hmm, that doesn't work either because \"Palmeiras-SP\" (Brasileirao file) vs \"Palmeiras\" (Libertadores file) must map to the same team. And \"Atlético-MG\" vs \"Atletico Mineiro\" (BR-Football) must also map to the same team!\n\nSo we need a canonical registry. Build it from data:\n\n1. Collect all raw team names from all sources with their (base, uf) decomposition.\n2. The disambiguation problem: \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atlético-GO\", \"Atlético-PR\"/\"Athletico-PR\", \"América-MG\", \"América-RN\", \"Sport-PE\"...\n\nA curated alias map is honestly the standard solution for Brazilian soccer data. The set of teams is finite and well-known. Let me generate the list of distinct team names across all files, then write a canonical mapping with:\n\n- For names like \"Atlético-MG\" → canonical \"Atlético Mineiro\" (atletico-mg)\n- \"Atlético-GO\" → \"Atlético Goianiense\" (atletico-go)\n- \"Athletico-PR\"/\"Atlético-PR\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\" (athletico-pr)... note both spellings appear in different files (\"Atlético-PR\" in Brasileirao file, \"Athletico-PR\" in novo file!). Let me check.\n\nLet me enumerate all distinct team names and their frequency across files to build the registry. Then hardcode a curated map + generic fallback for unlisted names.\n\nLet me dump all distinct normalized base names per file.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dee1abe0017mHXedfct4VOK2","sessionID":"ses_fa214f21cffeb5QAv8JGSE5SjQ","messageID":"msg_05dede5e9001izfDpP9NPWd8sv"}}
