strip leading/trailing tokens in {ec, fc, sc, ac} only when they're separate tokens AND the remaining base is non-empty AND... \"SC Braga\", \"FC Porto\" are foreign. For match data, club-legal tokens appear in FIFA clubs and Copa do Brasil small clubs (\"Aquidauanense Futebol Clube - MS\", \"Operario Ferroviario Esporte C - PR\"). For Copa do Brasil, the UF suffix is present so key = base-with-junk + uf... e.g. \"operario ferroviario esporte c-pr\". Ugly but unique — fine for identity. It only needs to match if a USER queries that club; fuzzy substring match will handle \"operario\" → several \"operario-*\" keys... disambiguate by prominence. Good enough.\n\nBut stripping \"fc\"/\"ec\" tokens helps unify \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\" → auto-merge into \"bahia-ba\" (base \"bahia\" unique UF-variant). And \"Fortaleza FC\" (BR-Football) → \"fortaleza\" → \"fortaleza-ce\". \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"botafogo-rj\". \n\nWait — one risk: stripping \"sc\" token: \"Sampaio Correa\"? No \"SC\" there. What about a club literally named \"SC\"? No. OK.\n\nAlso FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\": clean removes parens → \"america fc\" → strip \"fc\" → \"america\" → auto-merge → \"america-mg\" (prominent) — but wait, could merge to \"america-rn\"! Bare \"america\" → most prominent UF variant = \"america-mg\" (Série A). Good. But that's for the FIFA club which IS América-MG. Correct!\n\nBut for the auto-merge of bare keys FROM DATA (not queries): \"america\" appears as a raw key only if some file has bare \"America\" without UF... BR-Football has \"America MG\" → \"america-mg\" after cleaning. Fine.\n\nNow — the crucial question of which base-UF keys to merge when multiple exist: bare \"atletico\" → variants \"atletico-mg\", \"atletico-go\", \"atletico-pr\" (athletico is separate), \"atletico-es\", \"atletico-ba\"... Most prominent = atletico-mg. But NO file uses bare \"Atletico\" without UF, so this only affects user queries. For user queries, prominence-based resolution + alternatives list i