\"goals_for\", \"goals_against\", \"win_rate\", \"biggest_win\"?}.\n\nstandings: {\"competition\", \"season\", \"table\": [{position, team, points, wins, draws, losses, goals_for, goals_against, goal_diff}], \"champion\", \"note\"}.\n\nchampion: league → top of table; cup → final winner.\n\nFor cup finals (Copa do Brasil): matches in max round of season; aggregate two legs; winner = higher aggregate; tie → None with note. Libertadores: stage == 'final' rows.\n\nrelegated: bottom N of league table.\n\nleague_averages: {\"matches\", \"home_wins\", \"away_wins\", \"draws\", \"avg_goals_per_match\", \"home_win_rate\", ...}.\n\nbiggest_wins: sorted by margin desc, then by total goals.\n\nbest_records: for venue home/away, win_rate ranking with min matches filter.\n\nderbies: {\"derbies\": [{\"name\": \"Fla-Flu\", \"teams\": [...], \"matches\": [...]}] or flat match list with derby names}.\n\nlist_competitions: [{\"competition\", \"seasons\": [min..max], \"match_count\", \"sources\": [...]}]\n\nsearch_teams: {\"query\", \"matches\": [{\"id\", \"display_name\", \"match_count\", \"competitions\"}]} — resolution helper.\n\nteam_profile: {\"team\", \"record\": {...overall...}, \"by_competition\": [...], \"players\": [...FIFA...], \"top_rated_player\": ...} — cross-file.\n\nsearch_players: filters name (substring, accent-insensitive), nationality exact-ish, club (registry-resolved + substring fallback), position, min_overall; order by overall desc.\n\nplayer_profile: full player dict + club canonical resolution.\n\nNow write the BDD tests (given/when/then). Structure each test with comments \"# Given / # When / # Then\" to mirror gherkin. Cover the 6 success criteria + the spec's example questions. At least 20 sample questions — I'll write ~60+ test cases total including a parametrized \"sample questions\" test module that mirrors the spec's question table.\n\nPerformance tests: timing assertions (simple lookup < 2s, aggregate < 5s) with generous margins.\n\nE2E MCP protocol tests: initialize, tools/list (expect all tools), tools/call search_matches + call_tool error path (unknown tool / bad args → proper error). \n\nNow — check `call_tool` error semantics in 2.x for invalid args (should raise ToolError in server → client gets isError). For robustness, my tools catch lookup failures and return {\"error\": ...}? Better: raise ValueError → SDK converts to tool error. For missing team names, return a helpful \"error\" + suggestions rather than exception, since LLM clients benefit from suggestions. I'll return {\"error\": msg, \"suggestions\": [...]} with 200 OK. Hmm, mixed philosophy; for name resolution I'll do suggestions, for programmer errors let it raise.\n\nLet me now also double check the mcp 2.x tool decorator: how does it serialize return values? If function returns dict → structuredContent. If returns str → text. I'll return dicts everywhere for consistency. Check `structured_output` param — default auto. Let me check the ToolManager behavior quickly in the spike (call add returning dict).\n\nOne more design point — the MCPServer constructor: `MCPServer(name=\"brazilian-soccer-mcp\", title=..., description=..., version=\"1.0.0\", instructions=...)`. And `run_stdio_async`.\n\nAlso `mcp.settings` — log level: default INFO; stdio logging writes to stderr — fine, must NOT pollute stdout.\n\nLet me now check how tool decorator handles type hints and docstrings (they become the schema). Also confirm CallToolResult field name: `structured_content`.\n\nTime to write the code. Let me write the modules now.\n\nFirst `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py`. Key components:\n\n```python\nBRAZILIAN_UFS = {\"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\"PA\",\"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"}  # lowercase set\n\nFOREIGN_MARKERS = {\"uru\",\"par\",\"equ\",\"arg\",\"chi\",\"col\",\"per\",\"bol\",\"ven\",\"mex\",\"usa\",\"uru\",\"jpn\",\"kor\",\"gtm\",\"crc\",\"hon\",\"slv\",\"pan\",\"can\"}  # lowercase; seen in Libertadores data\n\ndef strip_accents(s): ...\n\ndef clean_name(raw) -> (tokens)\ndef extract_uf(tokens) -> (base_tokens, uf)\ndef extract_country(tokens) -> (base_tokens, country)\n```\n\nAlgorithm for `team_key_from_name(raw, uf_hint=None)`:\n1. s = strip_accents(raw).lower()\n2. remove parenthetical content but REMEMBER it (may contain country or \"Minas Gerais\")\n3. replace non-alnum with space; collapse\n4. tokens; remove filler tokens: {\"antigo\", \"de\", ...}? No — \"Vasco da Gama\" needs \"da\"; keep small words. Remove {\"antigo\"} only. Also remove trailing club-form tokens {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"ac\",\"aa\"}? Only trailing single instance? \"Operario Ferroviario Esporte C - PR\" → \"operario ferreoviario esporte c-pr\"... trailing token before UF is \"c\" (truncated \"Clube\"). Keep as-is; uniqueness is fine.\n5. If last token in UFS → uf = that, base = rest. elif uf_hint provided (from state columns) → uf = hint. elif last token in FOREIGN_MARKERS → country = it, base = rest.\n6. key = \"-\".join(base) + (\"-\" + uf if uf else \"\") + (\"-\" + country if country else \"\")\n\nWait, for foreign teams WITHOUT markers (\"Boca Juniors\", \"River Plate\") → key \"boca juniors\", \"river plate\". Uniqueness: \"river plate\" vs Brazilian \"River-PI\" → \"river-pi\" distinct ✓. FIFA \"River Plate\"? No. OK.\n\nBut hmm: uf_hint from novo columns (\"SP\" etc.). For \"Guarani\" + hint \"SP\" → \"guarani-sp\" ✓. For Brasileirao file the name already has suffix; hint as backup.\n\nSpecial: \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → base \"sao paulo\" ✓. \"Atletico-GO\" → \"atletico-go\" ✓ distinct from \"atletico-mg\". \n\nCurated ALIASES (exact key → canonical key) for cross-file unification of full names:\n```python\nALIASES = {\n  \"atletico mineiro\": \"atletico-mg\",\n  \"atletico mineiro-mg\": \"atletico-mg\",   # \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\"\n  \"atletico paranaense\": \"athletico-pr\",\n  \"athletico paranaense\": \"athletico-pr\",\n  \"athletico paranaense-pr\": \"athletico-pr\",\n  \"atletico-pr\": \"athletico-pr\",\n  \"atletico paranaense-pr\": \"athletico-pr\",\n  \"atletico goianiense\": \"atletico-go\",\n  \"sport recife\": \"sport-pe\",\n  \"sport club do recife\": \"sport-pe\",\n  \"nautico capibaribe\": \"nautico-pe\",\n  \"ceara sporting club\": \"ceara-ce\",\n  \"america fc\": \"america-mg\",        # from FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"\n  \"america fc minas gerais\": \"america-mg\",\n  \"gremio novorizontino\"? no...\n  \"red bull bragantino-sp\" → auto fine.\n  \"ec bahia\": \"bahia-ba\"? — cleaning strips trailing \"ec\"? If I strip club-form tokens from the END only when ≥2 tokens remain: \"ec bahia\" → \"bahia\" → auto-merge → \"bahia-ba\" ✓ (bare \"bahia\" unique UF variant \"bahia-ba\"). So no alias needed if token stripping works. But \"SC Braga\" → \"braga\" fine. \"FC Porto\" → \"porto\" fine.\n}\n```\n\nHmm wait, stripping trailing form tokens changes \"santos-sp\"? No, \"santos\" isn't a form token. Stripping only tokens in {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"ac\",\"cb\",\"cbf\",\"futebol\",\"clube\",\"esporte\",\"club\",\"do\"}? NO — too aggressive: \"Botafogo\" fine but \"Club Brugge\"?? Not in our data. \"esporte\" appears mid-name (\"Operario Ferroviario Esporte C\"). I'll strip ONLY a TRAILING/LEADING single token from {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"ac\"} when remaining ≥1 token. \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\" ✓. \"Fortaleza FC\" → \"fortaleza\" ✓. \"América FC\" → \"america\" ✓.\n\nAuto-merge rule (registry build): after computing all keys with counts, for each bare key B (no uf/country) with no UF-ful twin: find keys B-uf... wait I said it backwards. Let me restate:\n- For key \"bahia\" (bare) and key \"bahia-ba\" (uf-ful, same base) → merge bare into uf-ful (base = key minus suffix).\n- If multiple uf-ful twins (e.g. \"santos\" → \"santos-sp\", \"santos-ap\"): merge into most prominent (highest count). This only fires for in-data bare keys (Libertadores bare names, BR-Foot