iple canonical keys → ambiguous. \"atletico\" → atletico-mg, atletico-go, athletico-pr, atletico-ba?? (\"Atlético - BA\" appeared in collisions! small club) → ambiguous → keep UF in display ✓. \"flamengo\" → flamengo-rj, flamengo-pi → ambiguous! But display should still be \"Flamengo\" for RJ (the famous one). Refine: display strips UF when this canonical is the PROMINENT one for its base. flamengo-rj prominent → \"Flamengo\" ✓; flamengo-pi → \"Flamengo-PI\". atletico-mg prominent among atletico* → \"Atlético-MG\"?? stripping gives \"Atlético\" — BAD (ambiguous with others when prominent rule alone). Hmm.\n\nAlternative display rule: strip UF only if base is UNIQUE in registry (exactly one canonical with that base): \"palmeiras\" unique → \"Palmeiras\"; \"atletico\" not unique → keep \"Atlético-MG\"; \"flamengo\" not unique (rj, pi) → \"Flamengo-RJ\"?? The example output in spec says \"Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense\" without suffixes. Hmm, but \"Flamengo-RJ\" is also perfectly clear.\n\nCompromise: display strips UF if unique OR if the club's prominence ratio > 10:1 vs siblings (flamengo-rj vs flamengo-pi huge ratio). atletico-mg vs atletico-go ratio ~small → keep suffix. That gives: Flamengo, Fluminense, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Santos (sp vs ap — huge ratio → \"Santos\"), Grêmio, Internacional, Cruzeiro, Bahia, Vitória?? (ba vs es — maybe 4:1 → keep \"Vitória-BA\"... hmm ratio 4 < 10 → keep suffix — fine, honest), Botafogo (rj vs sp/pb → big ratio → \"Botafogo\"), Sport (\"sport-pe\" unique → \"Sport\"), Athletico-PR (\"athletico-pr\" unique base → \"Athletico-PR\"... base \"athletico\" unique? atletico-pr merged INTO athletico-pr, so \"athletico\" base has only this → display \"Athletico\"? Hmm no — base for atletico-mg is \"atletico\" too! atletico-mg, atletico-go, atletico-ba, atletico-es... and athletico-pr separately. \"athletico\" base unique (only athletico-pr) → display \"Athletico\"?? That's wrong-ish; real name is Athletico-PR. Ugh.\n\nSimplest DEFENSIBLE rule: display = most frequent RAW variant as it appears in data, EXCEPT strip trailing \" - UF\"/\"-UF\" when base is unique. For athletico-pr → most frequent raw... in novo it's \"Athletico-PR\" (bare? novo has 'Athletico-PR' with UF baked ✓). Base \"athletico\" unique → strip → \"Athletico\". Hmm \"Athletico\" alone is odd but acceptable? Actually NO. \n\nLet me reconsider: maybe rule = strip UF when base unique AND base not a \"generic-ish\" name? Overthinking. FINAL RULE: display keeps the UF suffix EXCEPT for a curated set of famous unambiguous clubs where stripping reads naturally. Actually simplest of all: display = the most frequent raw variant, cleaned to the form \"Name-UF\" or \" - UF\"→\"-UF\" (whitespace normalize). So \"Flamengo-RJ\", \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"São Paulo\", \"Boca Juniors\". Wait \"São Paulo\" (Libertadores bare) vs \"Sao Paulo-SP\" (Brasileirao). Most frequent raw across all files for sao paulo-sp: Brasileirao file dominates count (3800 rows) → \"Sao Paulo-SP\" (no accent, from that file!). Hmm, ugly (\"Sao\" without accent).\n\nBetter: curated DISPLAY overrides for the top ~40 clubs (\"Flamengo\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Grêmio\", ...) + fallback = most-frequent-raw-normalized. That's clean and honest. I'll curate display names for prominent clubs, rest use raw.\n\nOK. Time to write code. Also the query module needs competition canonicalization:\n\n```python\nCOMPETITIONS = {\n  \"brasileirao-serie-a\": \"Brasileirão Série A\",\n  \"brasileirao-serie-b\": \"Brasileirão Série B\",\n  \"brasileirao-serie-c\": \"Brasileirão Série C\",\n  \"copa-do-brasil\": \"Copa do Brasil\",\n  \"libertadores\": \"Copa Libertadores\",\n}\n```\nWith alias resolution for user input: \"Serie A\", \"Brasileirão\", \"brasileirao\" → serie-a; \"Copa do Brasil\"/\"copa\"; \"Libertadores\"/\"copa libertadores\"; BR-Football \"Copa do Brasil\" merges with the dedicated Copa file — SAME competition family → dedup across