e write all files now. I'll be careful about:\n- utf-8-sig everywhere\n- None-safe analytics\n- query date params as ISO strings\n\nAlso — spec says \"MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\" — natural language comes from the LLM which uses tools; tools take structured params. ✓ (The MCP host/LLM does NL→tool-call; our server provides tools.)\n\nWrite order: models.py, normalize.py, loader.py, queries.py, server.py, tests, requirements.\n\nLet me write models.py:\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n@dataclass\nclass Match:\n    date: date | None\n    season: int | None\n    competition: str          # canonical competition name\n    stage: str | None\n    home: str                 # canonical team id\n    away: str\n    home_goals: int | None\n    away_goals: int | None\n    venue: str | None\n    source: str\n    # extras from BR-Football\n    home_corners: int | None = None\n    away_corners: int | None = None\n    home_shots: int | None = None\n    away_shots: int | None = None\n    home_attacks: int | None = None\n    away_attacks: int | None = None\n\n    def to_dict(...)\n\n@dataclass\nclass Player:\n    ...\n```\n\nnormalize.py as designed. loader.py builds:\n- `matches: list[Match]` (deduped unified)\n- `by_competition: dict[str, list[Match]]`\n- `players: list[Player]`\n- `teams: TeamRegistry` (canonical → variants, counts, display)\n- convenience: `seasons` per competition.\n\nqueries.py functions taking `data: SoccerData`.\n\nTeam resolution in queries: `data.teams.resolve(\"Flamengo\")` → (canonical_id, alternatives). Raise `TeamNotFound` (with suggestions) if nothing.\n\nLet me now write the actual code files.\n\nFor the registry build, the auto-merge algorithm:\n\n```python\ndef build_registry(name_counts: dict[raw, count], uf_hints per raw?) \n```\n\nHmm, the key computation needs uf_hint per row not per raw name... The novo file has bare names + UF columns; the same raw \"Palmeiras\" in novo has hint SP. But in Libertadores \"Palmeiras\" has NO hint. So key computation is per (raw, hint) occurrence — I'll compute keys during loading (per row) into the registry: `registry.note(raw, count, uf_hint)`.\n\nRegistry internals:\n- `self._key_counts: Counter[canonical]`\n- `self._raw_to_key: dict[raw, canonical]` (memoized per raw+hint)\n- `self._base_index: dict[base, set[canonical]]`\n\nresolve(query) → ResolveResult(canonical, display, alternatives, confidence).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. key = key_from_name(query) (with hint=None)\n2. If key in registry: return it (exact). Also check ALIASES.\n3. base = base of key. If base in base_index with exactly 1 canonical → return it.\n4. If multiple → most prominent + alternatives.\n5. Fuzzy: for each canonical, base.startswith(query_base) or query_base in base → candidates; pick best difflib ratio.\n6. Else TeamNotFound with suggestions (top difflib matches over all canonicals).\n\nAlso for user query WITH explicit UF (\"Atlético-MG\") → key \"atletico-mg\" exact ✓.\n\nEdge: user queries \"Corinthians\" → key \"corinthians\" → base_index[\"corinthians\"] = {corinthians-sp} → unique ✓.\nUser queries \"Atletico\" → base_index[\"atletico\"] = {atletico-mg, atletico-go, atletico-ba, atletico-es?...} → most prominent atletico-mg + alternatives. Good UX for the LLM.\n\nNow — the FIFA club resolution: club param → try registry resolve; if the resolved canonical has no players (like flamengo-rj), ALSO try substring over raw club names? E.g. club=\"Flamengo\" resolves to flamengo-rj; FIFA clubs mapped via registry: \"Grêmio\"→gremio-rs. For flamengo-rj: 0 players — return empty with note \"no players at Flamengo in FIFA dataset\". That's the honest answer per spec (\"Filter FIFA data by Club containing 'Flamengo'\" → 0 results, and the tool response says so).\n\nWait — should I map FIFA clubs into the registry? \"Santos\" (FIFA) → santos-sp; \"Santos Laguna\" → \"santos laguna\" (unregistered bare key). I'll note FIFA club names into the registry with tiny counts (or skip noting; resolve via same key algorithm + aliases: \"Atlético Mineiro\" → alias → atletico-mg ✓; \"Sport Club do Recife\" → alias → sport-pe ✓; \"Chapecoense\" → base unique → chapecoense-sc ✓; \"Paraná\" → parana-pr ✓; \"Vitória\" → prominence → vitoria-ba ✓; \"Bahia\" → bahia-ba ✓; \"Botafogo\" → botafogo-rj ✓; \"Santos\" → santos-sp ✓; \"Internacional\" → internacional-rs ✓; \"Cruzeiro\" → cruzeiro-mg ✓; \"Fluminense\" → fluminense-rj ✓; \"Grêmio\" → gremio-rs ✓; \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → \"ceara sporting club\" → alias → ceara-ce ✓; \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"america fc\" → strip fc → \"america\" → prominence → america-mg ✓ (hmm — resolve() step 3: base_index[\"america\"] = {america-mg, america-rn} → prominence america-mg ✓); \"Atlético Paranaense\" → alias athletico-pr ✓.)\n\nSo FIFA club lookup = registry.resolve(club_name). Since club is a user filter, I'll ALSO fall back to substring matching over raw FIFA club strings if registry resolution fails (e.g. \"PSG\" → \"Paris Saint-Germain\"? substring \"psg\" not in name... skip; \"Paris\" → contains ✓).\n\nLet me write everything now. Also decide: `parse_bool`? Not needed. Venue param: Literal \"all\"|\"home\"|\"away\" via str with validation.\n\nAbout server.py tools — full list with schemas:\n\n1. search_matches(team, opponent, competition, season, date_from, date_to, stage, limit)\n2. head_to_head(team_a, team_b, competition, limit)\n3. last_meeting(team_a, team_b, competition)\n4. team_record(team, competition, season, venue)\n5. team_profile(team)\n6. standings(competition, season)\n7. champion(competition, season)\n8. finals(competition, season)\n9. relegated(competition, season, count)\n10. league_averages(competition, season)\n11. biggest_wins(competition, season, team, limit)\n12. best_records(competition, season, venue, min_matches, limit)\n13. derbies(season, competition)\n14. search_players(name, nationality, club, position, min_overall, max_overall, limit, order_by)\n15. player_profile(name)\n16. top_players(nationality, club, position, limit)\n17. club_players(club) — players at a club (cross-file with team_profile)... team_profile already includes players. Keep both? team_profile includes players list. Skip club_players. Actually \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" → search_players(club=\"Flamengo\") works. ✓\n18. list_competitions()\n19. search_teams(query, limit)\n\n19 tools. \n\nDerbies curated pairs (canonical ids):\n- \"Fla-Flu\": flamengo-rj, fluminense-rj\n- \"Clássico dos Milhões\": flamengo-rj, vasco da gama-rj\n- \"Clássico Vovô\": botafogo-rj, vasco da gama-rj\n- \"Choque-Rei\": corinthians-sp, sao paulo-sp\n- \"Majestoso\": corinthians-sp, palmeiras-sp\n- \"Clássico da Saudade\": palmeiras-sp, santos-sp\n- \"Gre-Nal\": gremio-rs, internacional-rs\n- \"Atletiba\": athletico-pr, coritiba-pr\n- \"Ba-Vi\": bahia-ba, vitoria-ba\n- \"Re-Pa\": remo-pa, paysandu-pa\n- \"Clássico-Rei\": ceara-ce, fortaleza-ce\n- \"Clássico dos Gigantes\"? sport-pe vs nautico-pe = \"Clássico dos Clássicos\". Add: sport-pe vs santa cruz-pe (\"Clássico dos Clássicos\" is Santa Cruz vs Sport? — hmm: \"Clássico dos Clássicos\" = Santa Cruz–Sport; \"Clássico das Multidões\" = Santa Cruz–Náutico). I'll include a reasonable, well-known set; keep 12.\n\nNow write the code. Also conftest with session fixture. BDD test names like `test_find_matches_between_two_teams` with Given/When/Then comments.\n\nTest assertions (verify against data!):\n- Flamengo vs Fluminense matches exist (both orders) in Brasileirão. Head-to-head counts: compute in test via the function, assert internal consistency (sum wins+draws+losses == matches where goals known).\n- Palmeiras 2023 matches: Série A 2023 comes from BR-Football (377 matches). Palmeiras played ~38. Assert > 30 matches, all season 2023, all competitions.\n- Copa do Brasil finals: round == max round of season. 2019 final: Athletico-PR vs Internacional? Let me verify from data during