n `counts[bare] <= counts[target]`: counts['avai'] (bare, from BR-Football Serie A/B/C... Avaí in Serie B 2014-2018 ~ 5×38=190 + Serie A 2019 38 + Serie B 2020-2023...) vs counts['avai-sc'] (Brasileirao 2019: 38, novo 2003-2019 various, Copa do Brasil...). Bare 'avai' likely has MORE rows → fold blocked by my <= condition. THE FIX: bare keys should ALWAYS fold into the suffixed twin (the bare spelling is just an alias; prominence only chooses WHICH twin). Remove the count condition — bare always folds when suffixed twins exist.\n\nWait, but is that always right? Bare key with in-data occurrences: \"Vitoria\" bare in BR-Football = Vitória-BA (verified by history earlier). Bare \"santos\" in Libertadores = Santos-SP ✓. Bare \"bahia\" BR-Football = Bahia-BA ✓. The risk case would be a bare spelling referring to the LESS prominent club — I can't think of one in this data (the bare spellings come from BR-Football/Libertadores/FIFA which use the famous club's bare name). And novo always provides UF hints. OK — always fold bare → most prominent suffixed twin.\n\nHmm wait, one more consideration: FIFA club names also go through canonical() but they're not noted into counts... they ARE resolved via base-fold in canonical() (the `twins` logic) which uses prominence — consistent.\n\nBut careful: always-fold could break a case where the suffixed twin is for a DIFFERENT club sharing the base... e.g. bare \"guarani\" → twins: guarani-sp, guarani-ce → most prominent = guarani-sp ✓ (Libertadores \"Guarani (PAR)\" → \"guarani-par\" foreign, distinct ✓; novo \"Guarani\"+SP hint → \"guarani-sp\" ✓).\n\nNow also the 'vasco-rj' 19 issue: BR-Football names Vasco as... let me check raw names. If BR-Football uses \"Vasco RJ\" → key \"vasco-rj\" — bare base \"vasco\" ≠ \"vasco-da-gama\". After my always-fold fix, \"vasco-rj\" still won't fold into \"vasco-da-gama-rj\" because base_name(\"vasco-rj\") = \"vasco\" and base_name(\"vasco-da-gama-rj\") = \"vasco-da-gama\" — different bases! I need an alias \"vasco-rj\" → \"vasco-da-gama-rj\". Let me check what BR-Football actually calls it. Similarly check other Série A clubs' BR-Football spellings that differ structurally:\n- \"Atletico Mineiro\" ✓ alias exists\n- \"Athletico Paranaense\" ✓ alias exists  \n- \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"botafogo-rj\" ✓ auto\n- \"America MG\" → \"america-mg\" ✓ auto\n- \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\" → fold → \"bahia-ba\" ✓ (after always-fold)\n- \"Fortaleza FC\" → \"fortaleza\" → fold ✓\n- \"Sport Recife\" ✓ alias\n- \"Nautico Capibaribe\" ✓ alias\n- \"Sao Paulo\" → \"sao-paulo\" bare → fold → \"sao-paulo-sp\" ✓\n- \"Avai\" → fold ✓\n- \"Csa\" → \"csa\" → fold → \"csa-al\" ✓\n- \"Gremio\" → fold ✓\n- \"Coritiba PR\"? Let me check. → \"coritiba-pr\" ✓ auto\n- \"Goias\" ✓ fold\n- \"Cuiaba MT\"? → auto ✓\n- \"Vasco RJ\"?? — need to check\n- \"Juventude RS\" → auto ✓\n- \"Sampaio Correa\"? → bare → fold \"sampaio-correa-ma\" ✓\n\nLet me dump ALL distinct BR-Football names and check which produce keys not in {canonical set from other files}. Also check the extra 2019 fixtures from BR-Football (13 Flamengo rows not deduped — different dates? BR-Football 2019 Serie A has 380 rows; if 25 of Flamengo's deduped fine...).\n\nActually the 53-38=15 extra Flamengo rows: 2 from novo + 13 from BR-Football with differing (date/score). These are data discrepancies (e.g. BR-Football dates might be off by a day, or scores differ). Let me inspect a few to decide policy. If BR-Football has wrong dates, dedup misses and standings DOUBLE-COUNT → wrong tables. That's serious for standings correctness.\n\nPolicy options:\na) Trust priority: for league standings, use ONE authoritative source per season: Brasileirao_Matches for 2012-2022, novo for 2003-2011, BR-Football for 2023. This guarantees correct standings without relying on cross-file dedup.\nb) Improve dedup: match on (season, home, away) ignoring date... but two legs per season (home/away reversed) — dedup on (home, away, season) + score equality... still risky.\n\nOption (a) is cleaner for standings. For match SEARCH queries, the unified deduped store is fine (occasional duplicate from data discrepancy acceptable; actually hmm — search would show both variants of the same fixture with different dates/scores — confusing but honest \"data has both records\").\n\nLet me look at the 15 Flamengo extras to understand the discrepancy type.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05df721000018hOiFG2uDUpDLP","sessionID":"ses_fa214f21cffeb5QAv8JGSE5SjQ","messageID":"msg_05df68cee001VnQsisHAqDzkwJ"}}
