 produce short-key mismatches? novo names: 'Guarani'(+SP), 'Vasco'(+RJ), 'Sport'(+PE), 'Grêmio'(+RS), 'Palmeiras'(+SP), 'Santos'(+SP), 'Bahia'(+BA), 'Ceará'(+CE)... most fold fine because the suffixed twin has the same base. The problem is only where the canonical name includes MORE words than novo's bare name (Vasco da Gama) or FEWER (Atlético-MG vs novo \"Atlético-MG\"?? novo has 'Atlético-MG' baked ✓).\n\nLet me enumerate novo bare names: from the novo team list: América-MG, América-RN, Athletico-PR, Atlético-GO, Atlético-MG, Avaí, Bahia, Barueri, Botafogo-RJ, Brasiliense, CSA, Ceará, Chapecoense, Corinthians, Coritiba, Criciúma, Cruzeiro, Figueirense, Flamengo, Fluminense, Fortaleza, Goiás, Grêmio, Grêmio Prudente, Guarani, Internacional, Ipatinga, Joinville, Juventude, Náutico, Palmeiras, Paraná, Paysandu, Ponte Preta, Portuguesa, Santa Cruz, Santo André, Santos, Sport, São Caetano, São Paulo, Vasco, Vitória...\n\nMost novo names have UF baked or fold correctly. Only \"Vasco\" is structurally different. Add alias \"vasco-rj\" → \"vasco-da-gama-rj\" (and also \"vasco\" bare → same, for user queries).\n\nAlso note BR-Football has BOTH 'Caxias' and 'Caxias RS' → 'caxias' / 'caxias-rs' — bare folds ✓. 'Duque De Caxias RJ' → 'duque-de-caxias-rj' vs 'Duque de Caxias FC' → 'duque-de-caxias' bare → folds ✓. 'Remo'/'Remo PA'/'Clube Do Remo' → 'remo' folds ✓, 'clube-do-remo' needs alias ✓ (already have). 'Vitoria EC' → 'vitoria' (EC stripped) ✓ folds to vitoria-ba? WAIT — \"EC Vitoria\" is Vitória-BA? or Vitória-ES?? BR-Football has 'EC Vitoria' AND 'Vitoria' AND 'Vitoria ES' AND 'Vitoria da Conquista'. Serie A 2018 Vitória-BA... 'Vitoria EC' probably = Vitória-BA (Esporte Clube Vitória). And plain 'Vitoria' too. Both fold to vitoria-ba (prominent) ✓ consistent.\n\n'Athletico Paranaense' AND 'Atletico Paranaense' both in BR-Football → both alias → athletico-pr ✓.\n\n'Bragantino' + 'Bragantino PA' → 'bragantino' (fold→bragantino-sp... wait twins: bragantino-pa exists! prominence: bragantino-sp in Série A/B (hundreds) vs bragantino-pa (few Copa matches) → bragantino-sp ✓) + alias chain bragantino-sp → red-bull-bragantino-sp.\n\nHmm wait — actually should I merge bragantino-sp into red-bull-bragantino-sp? The Copa file has \"Red Bull Bragantino - SP\" → 'red-bull-bragantino-sp'; BR-Football 'Bragantino' (2014-2018 Serie B) → 'bragantino-sp'. Same club continuing. For consistency in Série B standings 2014-2018 the club appears as bragantino-sp; 2019+ as red-bull-bragantino-sp. Merging makes h2h/team records span the lineage — I judge that desirable (\"Compare Bragantino records\"). Add alias 'bragantino-sp' → 'red-bull-bragantino-sp'.\n\nHmm, wait — but the alias fires in team_key which applies ALIASES to the computed key. For Brasileirao_Matches \"Bragantino-SP\"? Does that file contain Bragantino? 2019 Série A: \"Bragantino-SP\"?? no — 2019 Série A had \"RB Bragantino\"? Hmm, 2019 Série A: the file spells it... let me not guess. The collision list showed 'Red Bull Bragantino', 'Red Bull Bragantino - SP', 'Red Bull Bragantino-SP', 'Bragantino - PA', 'Bragantino - SP' — all exist across files. OK alias handles.\n\nAlso 'Coritiba PR' → 'coritiba-pr' ✓ auto. 'Cuiaba'/'Cuiaba MT' → ✓. 'Goias' ✓. 'Santos AP' → 'santos-ap' ✓ distinct. 'ABC' → 'abc' folds to 'abc-rn' ✓. 'CA Parana' → 'ca-parana' — needs alias → 'parana-pr'. 'Parana' → 'parana' folds → 'parana-pr' ✓. 'America FC Natal' → alias → 'america-rn'. 'CS Alagoano' → alias → 'csa-al'. 'CS Sergipe' → 'cs-sergipe' → alias 'sergipe-se'? Copa file \"Sergipe - SE\" → 'sergipe-se'. Add alias. 'Atletico Acreano' → alias 'atletico-ac'. 'Juventude MA' → 'juventude-ma' (distinct tiny club — actually Juventude-MA (Maranhão) exists in Copa do Brasil ✓ distinct from juventude-rs; keep separate — hmm 'EC Juventude' → 'juventude' → folds to juventude-rs ✓ (more prominent than juventude-ma ✓).\n\nOK. Now implement all fixes:\n\n**normalize.py fixes:**\n1. `merge_bare_keys`: always fold bare → suffixed (remove `<=` condition; keep only when suffixed twins exist).\n2. `canonical()`: apply ALIASES + redirect chase AFTER base-fold too.\n3. Add aliases: 'vasco-rj'→'vasco-da-gama-rj', 'vasco'→'vasco-da-gama-rj' (hmm — bare 'vasco' from FIFA? FIFA has no Vasco. From user queries \"Vasco\" → canonical: base 'vasco' → twins by base: 'vasco-da-gama-rj'? base_name('vasco-da-gama-rj') = 'vasco-da-gama' ≠ 'vasco'. So base-fold won't find it! Need alias 'vasco' → 'vasco-da-gama-rj'. ✓), 'bragantino-sp'→'red-bull-bragantino-sp', 'ca-parana'→'parana-pr', 'america-fc-natal'→'america-rn', 'cs-alagoano'→'csa-al', 'cs-sergipe'→'sergipe-se', 'atletico-acreano'→'atletico-ac', 'clube-do-remo'→'remo-pa' (already have 'clube-do-remo'? I added it above? No — I have 'sport-club-do-recife'. Add 'clube-do-remo'→'remo-pa'.)\n\nWait also — novo \"Vasco\" + hint RJ gives 'vasco-rj' via team_key... and ALIASES['vasco-rj'] → 'vasco-da-gama-rj' fires in team_key directly ✓.\n\n**loader.py fixes:**\n4. Two-level dedup: exact key + (competition, season, home, away, goals) within ±1 day.\n   Implementation: keep dict exact_key → Match (first). For fuzzy: dict (competition, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) → list of dates. On each new match: if exact key seen → skip. Else check fuzzy key: any existing date within 1 day → skip. Else add + record.\n   \n   Wait, season for BR-Football comes from date[:4] — the +1 day shift could push a Dec 31 match into next year... rare, fine.\n   \n   Hmm — one concern: legit different matches with same pairing+score within 1 day? Never in these comps. And two-legged cup ties: same pairing, same score, but dates apart by a week+ → both kept ✓. BUT what about the same fixture listed in BOTH Brazilian_Cup_Matches AND BR-Football Copa do Brasil with dates agreeing exactly → exact dedup ✓ (they mostly do).\n\n5. Source priority: process order already: Brasileirao, Copa, Libertadores, novo, BR-Football. For Série A 2012-2019 both Brasileirao & novo have exact dates mostly — dedup exact ✓. Wait, which is more authoritative? Either. Fine.\n\nActually — also need to double check: does BR-Football duplicate rows WITHIN itself (2021 Serie A 491 rows)? The fuzzy dedup will catch same pairing+score within a day. Different scores → both kept (data errors — 2021 has 491 rows; real = 380; extras might be data errors with different scores. Hmm, those would pollute 2021 standings!). Let me check 2021 Serie A specifically after the fix — count matches & teams. If still >380, investigate.\n\nAlso for 2020 Serie A BR-Football has 264 rows (partial) — fine, dedup against Brasileirao's 380 ✓ all absorbed? 2020 season: Brasileirao file has 2020 ✓ 380. So BR-Football 2020 absorbed ✓.\n\nNow — Série B: BR-Football is the ONLY source (3677 rows) ✓ no dedup issues. Série C same.\n\nCopa do Brasil: Brazilian_Cup (1337) + BR-Football Copa (1123) — overlap 2014-2023. Earlier count showed Copa do Brasil unified = 2276 (1337+1123=2460 → 184 deduped). With fuzzy ±1 day, more will dedup.\n\nLet me implement and validate against known champions 2012-2022 + Série A season counts (should be ~380 per season; 2003-2005 have more teams: 2003/2004 = 462/552 (24 teams), 2005 = 462 (22 teams)).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05df82cd1001iLM7odCT9oTfRF","sessionID":"ses_fa214f21cffeb5QAv8JGSE5SjQ","messageID":"msg_05df7c5360019aHH2750y67yxC"}}
