" → sport-pe ✓. \"Guarani\" → guarani-sp ✓ (novo Guarani = Campinas ✓). \"Paraná\" → parana-pr ✓. \"Santos\" → santos-sp ✓. \"América\"? — novo América-MG baked ✓ no bare. \"Botafogo-RJ\" baked ✓. Looks safe — novo clubs are the famous ones where prominence works.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety: WITHOUT hints, in pass 1 the noted key is bare \"vitoria\" (count += ~38 from novo) which then FOLDS into \"vitoria-ba\" ✓. The phantom disappears. \n\nHmm, but there's one more consideration: without hints, could two DIFFERENT novo clubs collide into the same bare key? E.g. if novo had both \"América-MG\" and \"América-RN\" — baked ✓ distinct. Fine.\n\nSo: novo hint = None. Simple. Let me also drop the hint for the \"Bahia BH\" typo (same fix — the hint \"BH\" isn't in UFS anyway → ignored ✓... wait \"BH\" not in BRAZILIAN_UFS → hint ignored → bare \"bahia\" → folds ✓).\n\nNow for bragantino-pa in BR-Football: per-file override {\"Bragantino PA\": \"Red Bull Bragantino\"} in the loader. Apply BEFORE normalization for BR-Football rows. But careful — the Copa file's \"Bragantino - PA\" (real Pará club) stays ✓.\n\nWait, one more check — the 2020 phantom analysis said extras == bragantino-pa count (27). But there were also 2020 teams at 39/40 — the 27 phantom matches inflated them. After the fix, 2020 should be 380. And Fortaleza 2020? \"Fortaleza FC\"? no that folds fine.\n\nAlso 2014/2016/2017 had 402-404 — let me recheck after fixes. And 2021's 30 junk fixtures (BR-Football misdated+wrong scores) — those remain (dates months apart, different scores). Hmm: 2021 = 458 matches = 380 + 30 junk (from the dups listing) + 48?? Let me recount after fixes.\n\nFor 2021: BR-Football junk rows. Strategy: drop BR-Football rows for (competition, season) combos already FULLY covered by a more authoritative source. Better general principle: for Série A, BR-Football only ADDS value for seasons NOT covered by Brasileirao/novo files (i.e., 2023) + extended stats (corners/shots) for matches. So: for Série A seasons covered by Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022), skip BR-Football Série A rows entirely? But then I lose corner/shot stats attached to those matches... The stats enrichment is a nice-to-have; correctness of the match store matters more.\n\nBetter approach: SOURCE PRIORITIZATION per (competition, season):\n- Série A: Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022) authoritative; novo for 2003-2011; BR-Football only for seasons not covered (2023).\n- Série B/C: BR-Football only source ✓.\n- Copa do Brasil: Brazilian_Cup_Matches (2012-2021); BR-Football covers 2014-2023 → use BR-Football only for uncovered seasons (2022-2023).\n- Libertadores: single source.\n\nBut then BR-Football's extended stats (corners/shots/attacks) are LOST for overlapping seasons. Do I care? The spec mentions the columns but the required capabilities don't demand per-match corner stats. I keep them for the matches that DO come from BR-Football (Série B/C, 2022-23 Copa, 2023 Série A). That's still \"all 6 CSVs loadable and queryable\" ✓ (BR-Football contributes Série B/C + 2023 + stats).\n\nHmm — but wait: \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" for 2022-2023 → from BR-Football ✓ works.\n\nIs there a risk that dropping BR-Football rows for covered seasons loses matches NOT in the primary files? E.g. Copa do Brasil 2014: Brazilian_Cup has 159 matches, BR-Football Copa 2014 has 43 — subset presumably. Série A 2014: both 380 ✓ complete coverage. Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2022 always 380/season ✓ complete. novo 2003-2011 complete ✓. So per-season authority works.\n\nImplementation: loader pass 2 becomes source-aware:\n1. Build a coverage map: for each (competition, season), the set of sources with rows, and pick the authoritative source per known hierarchy: {Brasileirao_Matches > novo > BR-Football} for Série A; {Brazilian_Cup_Matches > BR-Football} for Copa; Libertadores sole.\n   Actually simpler hierarchy: source_priority = {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 0, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 1, 'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv': 0, 'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 0, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 2}. For each (competition, season): determine which sources have ≥ some threshold... hmm, what if the authoritative source has PARTIAL coverage of a season (novo 2005 has 462 — full for 22 teams ✓)?\n\n   Rule: for each (competition, season), use only rows from the single best-priority source that has rows for that key. BR-Football used only when no better source covers that (competition, season).\n\n   Edge: Série A 2003-2011 → only novo ✓. 2012-2022 → Brasileirao ✓. 2023 → BR-Football ✓. Copa 2012-2021 → Brazilian_Cup ✓; 2022-2023 → BR-Football ✓. Série B/C all seasons → BR-Football ✓. \n\n   What about (competition= Serie A, season) present in Brasileirao AND BR-Football only for SOME rows — e.g. does Brasileirao_Matches cover ALL 2012-2022? Yes 380 each.\n\n2. Then within the chosen source's rows, still dedup exact duplicates (BR-Football 2021 491 rows → within-source dups!). For 2023 Série A (BR-Football only): 377 rows — dedup within-source exact + fuzzy ±1 day.\n\nHmm wait — but for 2021 BR-Football junk (misdated Jan 2021 rows with wrong scores): if BR-Football is skipped entirely for Série A 2021 ✓ problem gone. For BR-Football-only seasons (2023 Série A): is there junk? 377 matches ≈ complete-ish. Teams at 37 → partial data (missing matches), no phantom duplication. Fine — note in standings.\n\nBut Série B 2021 BR-Football has 446 rows (expected 380) — junk within the ONLY source! Within-source fuzzy dedup (±1 day, same pairing+score) may not catch junk with different scores/dates. Hmm. Let me check Série B 2021 duplicates... 446-380 = 66 extras. Let me analyze. If they're misdated junk with distinct scores, I can't dedup them safely. Options: detect league-season integrity: for a double round-robin, each ordered pair plays exactly once. I could enforce: within (competition=league, season, home, away) keep only ONE match — the one from... hmm, if two different matches exist 