son?? Série B 2020 (COVID) ran until January 2021! YES — Série B 2020 finished in January 2021. So these \"2021-01\" rows are REAL 2020-season matches! My season extraction (date[:4]) mislabels them as 2021. That explains everything: Série B 2020 = 302 rows (partial in BR-Football — also COVID-affected season with 381 games), and the Jan 2021 rows belong to season 2020!\n\nCheck: Série B 2020 rows = 302. 380 - 302 = 78 missing. And 2021-01 rows = 67. Hmm close. And \"Serie A\" 2021 = 491 rows: Série A 2020 ended Jan 2021?? No wait — Série A 2020 ended Feb 2021 (Flamengo champion Feb 25, 2021). So Série A \"2021-01\" + \"2021-02\" rows are really season-2020 tail! Let me verify: BR-Football Serie A by month for label-2021: earlier I saw 2021 Flamengo junk dated 2021-01-07 — season 2020's last rounds were Jan-Feb 2021 ✓!! And Serie A 2020 = 264 rows (partial) + Jan/Feb-2021 rows = complete-ish 2020.\n\nSo the correct interpretation: BR-Football rows in Jan/Feb of year Y+1 belong to season Y (COVID-era 2020/2021). Since Brasileirao_Matches covers Série A 2020-2022 with proper season labels, BR-Football's mislabeled rows are skipped anyway for Série A. For Série B: BR-Football is the ONLY source; season attribution by date[:4] mislabels Jan-2021 rows as 2021 instead of 2020.\n\nFix for Série B (and C, cups): season attribution needs to handle Jan/Feb. General rule for BR-Football: rows in Jan/Feb of year Y belong to season Y-1? NO — that's only true for the COVID seasons (2020, 2021). Normally (2014-2019, 2022-2023), Série B starts April. A Jan/Feb row for those years would be... state championships (not in this dataset) — so any Jan/Feb BR-Football row here IS COVID-era. Let me check month distribution across years for Serie B/C/Copa in BR-Football: are there Jan/Feb rows outside 2021/2022 labels? Let me check. If Jan/Feb rows only occur for labels 2021/2022 (seasons 2020/2021 tails), the rule \"month in {01,02} → season = year - 1\" is safe for BR-Football.\n\nWait — but hold on: season 2021's tail: Série B 2021 ended Nov 2021 (normal) ✓ no spillover. Série A 2021 ended Dec ✓. But Série C 2021? ended normal. Copa do Brasil 2021 ended Oct/Nov ✓. So only 2020 had the Jan/Feb 2021 tail. And 2021-02 label rows for Série A = season 2020 tail (Série A 2020 ended Feb 2021!). Let me verify month distributions per tournament per label-year to confirm.\n\nActually — also Série A 2020 label: 264 rows. If 2020 label rows are May-Dec 2020 (partial — missing the Jan/Feb 2021 tail which is labeled 2021), then 264 + Jan/Feb-2021 rows = full 380? Earlier: Série A label-2021 = 491 rows = real 380 (May-Dec 2021) + 111 (Jan/Feb 2021 = season 2020 tail). 264 + 111 = 375 ≈ 380 (5 missing — data holes). OK!\n\nSo the fix: in BR-Football parsing, if month is 01 or 02, season = year - 1. Let me confirm no Jan/Feb rows in non-COVID label years.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dfa88d9001N4CN1u4DDheCpJ","sessionID":"ses_fa214f21cffeb5QAv8JGSE5SjQ","messageID":"msg_05dfa45f1001hDcWKtjWTHHBj1"}}
