e 13, in main` → `res3.structured_content.get`. If line 11-12 had failed, the traceback would point there. So lines 11-12 SUCCEEDED (prints buffered but lost when process exited via exception? stdout is line-buffered when tty, block-buffered when piped... the timeout command pipes → block buffering → prints lost on hard exit? Actually python flushes stdout at exit even on exception — unless the anyio task group cancellation killed things. Whatever.)\n\nConclusion: with `-> dict`, valid results DO produce structured content (model for `dict` annotation exists). Then why did `{\"error\": ...}` NOT get structured content? Look at convert_result: `output_model is None → return CallToolResult(content=unstructured_content)`. If output_model existed, error dict would validate fine...\n\nHmm wait — look again at the docstring in the Tool class around `structured_output=None` (auto): \"Content blocks and the Image/Audio helpers are what the model reads\". And in `Tool.__init__` maybe auto mode disables schema for untyped dict... \n\nLet me just empirically determine: run two calls and print structured for both.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e04e891001EG4JcBu2k29o65","sessionID":"ses_fa214f21cffeb5QAv8JGSE5SjQ","messageID":"msg_05e04a6ee0019t3rxy3FzMuyWA"}}
